      "response": "A `cache_key` must include model identity because the same prompt can produce different results on different models.\n\nWhy:\n- Different models have different weights, tokenizers, context limits, and decoding behavior.\n- Even the same model family can change across versions.\n- So if the `cache_key` only uses the prompt, you could return a cached answer from the wrong model.\n\nExample:\n- Prompt: “Summarize this text”\n- Model A: concise summary\n- Model B: detailed summary\n\nIf both share the same `cache_key`, the cache may serve the wrong response.\n\nSo the `cache_key` should include at least:\n- prompt/input\n- model name or ID\n- model version or revision\n- relevant generation settings if they affect output\n\nThis keeps cached results correct and avoids cross-model collisions.",
