      "response": "A `cache_key` must include model identity because the same input can produce different outputs on different models.\n\nWhy:\n- Different models have different tokenization, context limits, system behavior, and decoding.\n- A response cached for one model may be wrong, invalid, or unsafe for another.\n- Without model identity in the `cache_key`, two models can collide and reuse the wrong result.\n\nSo the `cache_key` should distinguish:\n- model name/version\n- prompt/input\n- relevant generation settings\n\nIn short: same prompt ≠ same result unless the model is the same.",
